    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73928" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμπν-η</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>food, bread-corn,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διόνυσον ὄμπνῃ συντίθησιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sosith.
					2.11
				</span></i>
			 (cj. <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίνυσι τ᾽ ἔμπης,</span>
			dub.) : in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμπναι,</span>
			<i>cakes of meal and honey, sacrificial cakes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				268
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυωπέας ὄμπνας</span>”
				<i>honeycombs,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					450
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμπας</span> codd. opt. and
			Sch.). (The form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμπη</span> is found in <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				287
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">Phot.,
					<u>EM</u>625.52</span></i>.)
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμπνη: τροφή, εὐδαιμονία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
